# Idiomatic API cheatsheet

Each task twice: with the idiomatic structs, and with the generated
`ExPoser.Api` on handles. Frames are PoserPython's, from 0: `frame: 4` is GUI
frame 5.

## Get a figure
{: .col-2}

### Idiomatic

```elixir
{:ok, fig} = ExPoser.Scene.figure("Figure 1")
# internal or display name; nothing to release
```

### ExPoser.Api

```elixir
{:ok, scene} = ExPoser.Api.scene()
{:ok, fig} = ExPoser.Api.SceneType.figure(scene, "Figure 1")
# ...
ExPoser.Client.release([scene, fig])
```

## Read a dial
{: .col-2}

### Idiomatic

```elixir
{:ok, bend} = ExPoser.Figure.parameter(fig, "Left Forearm", "Bend")
{:ok, 0.0} = ExPoser.Parameter.value(bend)
```

### ExPoser.Api

```elixir
{:ok, arm} = ExPoser.Api.FigureType.actor(fig, "Left Forearm")
{:ok, bend} = ExPoser.Api.ActorType.parameter(arm, "Bend")
{:ok, 0.0} = ExPoser.Api.ParmType.value(bend)
ExPoser.Client.release([arm, bend])
```

## Set a dial at a frame
{: .col-2}

### Idiomatic

```elixir
{:ok, :ok} = ExPoser.Parameter.set_value(bend, 30.0, frame: 4)
# the current frame is restored
```

### ExPoser.Api

```elixir
{:ok, orig} = ExPoser.Api.SceneType.frame(scene)
{:ok, nil} = ExPoser.Api.SceneType.set_frame(scene, 4)
{:ok, nil} = ExPoser.Api.ParmType.set_value(bend, 30.0)
{:ok, nil} = ExPoser.Api.SceneType.set_frame(scene, orig)
```

## Set many dials
{: .col-2}

### Idiomatic

```elixir
# one request
ExPoser.Actor.set(arm, %{"yrot" => 30.0, "xrot" => -10.0})

# across actors and frames, one request
ExPoser.batch!(fn b ->
  b
  |> ExPoser.Batch.set(bend, 30.0, frame: 4)
  |> ExPoser.Batch.set(twist, -10.0, frame: 4)
end)
```

### ExPoser.Api

```elixir
# one request per call
{:ok, bend} = ExPoser.Api.ActorType.parameter(arm, "Bend")
{:ok, twist} = ExPoser.Api.ActorType.internal_parameter(arm, "xrot")  # "Twist" labels two dials
{:ok, nil} = ExPoser.Api.ParmType.set_value(bend, 30.0)
{:ok, nil} = ExPoser.Api.ParmType.set_value(twist, -10.0)
ExPoser.Client.release([bend, twist])
```

## List keyframes
{: .col-2}

### Idiomatic

```elixir
{:ok, [0, 4]} = ExPoser.Parameter.keyframes(bend)
```

### ExPoser.Api

```elixir
# NextKeyFrame reads from the current frame,
# so walk the timeline and put it back
{:ok, orig} = ExPoser.Api.SceneType.frame(scene)

keys =
  Stream.unfold(0, fn f ->
    ExPoser.Api.SceneType.set_frame(scene, f)

    case ExPoser.Api.ParmType.next_key_frame(bend) do
      {:ok, nil} -> nil
      {:ok, next} -> {next, next}
    end
  end)
  |> Enum.to_list()

ExPoser.Api.SceneType.set_frame(scene, orig)
[0 | keys]
```

## Get a handle
{: .col-2}

### Idiomatic

```elixir
{:ok, h} = ExPoser.Parameter.handle(bend)
ExPoser.Api.ParmType.min_value(h)
ExPoser.Client.release([h])
```

### ExPoser.Api

```elixir
# every ExPoser.Api result that is a
# Python object is already a handle
%ExPoser.Handle{class: "ParmType"} = bend
```

## Frames and names
{: .col-2}

### Frames

| PoserPython / `frame:` | GUI |
|---|---|
| `0` | 1 |
| `4` | 5 |
| `num_frames - 1` | last |

### Names

| Struct field | Poser |
|---|---|
| `internal` | `InternalName()`, the path key |
| `name` | `Name()`, the GUI label |
| `inspect/1` | shows `internal` |
